## Initial Q&A
### What was the U.S. GDP growth rate reported on or around October 29-30, 2020, and what specific measure (e.g., annualized quarterly rate, year-over-year) did it represent?
Answer: The U.S. GDP grew at a record **annualized rate of 33.1%** in the third quarter of 2020 (July–September), as reported by the Commerce Department on October 29, 2020. The government reports GDP "as an annualized number," which means the quarterly change is multiplied to project what the growth would be over a full year; on a non-annualized basis, the quarterly growth was actually 7.4%.

