Answer: Based on the search result, the previous highest quarterly GDP growth rate on record was 3.9% in the first quarter of 1950, which would now rank as the second-highest after Q3 2020's 7.4% quarterly rate. The source states this 3.9% was "almost half of this historic high." Numerically comparing to 33.1% (the annualized figure Trump cited), 3.9% is roughly one-eighth of 33.1%, making Trump's claim that the 33.1% figure was "almost triple" the previous record an understatement—it's actually more than eight times larger when comparing annualized rates.

